      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: instead of restricted, can we implement this as allowed?\n\nI think the set of allowed for a specific container will be smaller than the set of restricted, which will make it more maintainable. \n\ne.g. In the current implementation, system only has vendor in its restricted. Should product, apex, ... be in the restricted list of system as well?",
