      "writtenOn": "2024-07-01T18:27:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that we are newly introducing an enforcement, I\u0027d prefer explicit listing of all restrictions over all possible combinations except exceptions (i.e. allowlist). This allows new enforcement to be incrementally added in the future if necessary, and the current implementation of restriction to error message mapping allows informing users about why the dependency is disallowed and how to satisfy the restriction (e.g. depending on the stubs or HALs) IMO.\n\n\u003e e.g. In the current implementation, system only has vendor in its restricted. Should product, apex, ... be in the restricted list of system as well?\n\nI do not have a clear answer for this question. IIUC the purpose of this restriction is not to restrict all inter-container dependencies, but to restrict inter-container dependencies of interest. I believe that the restrictions explicitly listed here reflect the \"interest\".",
      "parentUuid": "5907b158_04d95d46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "0ddc4de334ff56b923b03e1888352d24b8369ca9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
